* RNG entropy\nincident
** The symptom
*** seeds ~72 bits\n(Mk4/Mk5/Q)
*** seeds ~40 bits\n(Mk3 >= 4.0.1)
*** target 128 bits
*** regenerate advised
** The mechanism
*** MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_RNG = 0
*** upstream rng.c compiles\nsoftware PRNG
*** board rng.c lacked\nrng_get()
*** linker resolved to\nyasmarang
** The call chain
*** seed.py generate_seed
*** ngu.random.bytes
*** CHIP_TRNG_32 = rng_get
*** XOR with second\nPRNG
** Why XOR did not save it
*** both halves\ndeterministic
*** libngu pad reseeded\nwith 32 bits
*** SE entropy truncated\nto 4 bytes
*** sha256d adds\nno entropy
** The fix
*** empty upstream rng.o
*** board exports rng_get
*** nm assertion in\nthe build
*** build fails on\nregression
